<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the first</p>
<p>day of four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Wednesday:</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham v Hampshire - no play due to</p>
<p>rain.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex 280 (D.Robinson 78, P.Prichard 51;</p>
<p>J.Kerr 4-83). Somerset 42-2.</p>
<p>At Swansea: Glamorgan 19-0 v Gloucestershire.</p>
<p>At Maidstone: Kent 306 (N.Llong 57, P.Strang 55; M Akram</p>
<p>4-56) v Northamptonshire.</p>
<p>At Leicester: Yorkshire 149-5 (D. Byas 66 not out) v</p>
<p>Leicestershire.</p>
<p>At Uxbridge: Middlesex 118 (P.Martin 8-32). Lancashire 126-0</p>
<p>(N. Wood 67 not out).</p>
<p>At Arundel: Worcestershire 185-8 v Sussex.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Surrey 157-6 v Warwickshire.</p>
</text>
